---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="NO BALL GAMES | Street Culture, Grime Art & Digital Collectibles"
  description="NO BALL GAMES is a street-culture brand built from graffiti energy, restricted spaces, underground creativity, digital collectibles, and community rebellion."
  current="home"
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-card hero-copy">
      <span class="eyebrow">Street culture • Grime art • Digital rebellion</span>
      <h1>NO BALL <span class="hero-title-accent">GAMES</span></h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Not just a sign. A symbol of restricted spaces, broken rules, estate culture, street creativity, and turning limitation into identity.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="button primary" href={`${base}projects/`}>Enter the movement</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href={`${base}about/`}>Read the story</a>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-grid" aria-label="Brand pillars">
        <div class="stat"><strong>01</strong><span>Street-rooted identity</span></div>
        <div class="stat"><strong>02</strong><span>Art, lore and culture</span></div>
        <div class="stat"><strong>03</strong><span>Collectibles and community</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <aside class="hero-card hero-sign" aria-label="NO BALL GAMES sign graphic">
      <div class="restricted-board">
        <strong>NO BALL</strong>
        <strong>GAMES</strong>
        <span>Play anyway</span>
      </div>
      <p>
        Built from the places where creativity was told to keep quiet. Walls, estates, signs, tags, characters, collectibles and stories — all pushed into one brand system.
      </p>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>Built from the ban</h2>
      <p>NO BALL GAMES takes a dead public warning and turns it into a creative operating system: art, clothing, lore, collectibles, gaming ideas and community culture.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Identity</span>
        <h3>From restriction to symbol</h3>
        <p>The phrase carries the feeling of being told where not to play, where not to create and where not to belong. The brand flips that message into ownership.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Art</span>
        <h3>Graffiti and grime energy</h3>
        <p>Raw mark-making, street typography, worn textures, pop-culture attitude and hand-painted edge form the visual backbone of the project.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Digital</span>
        <h3>Collectible-ready universe</h3>
        <p>The site is structured to support character drops, lore pages, digital collectibles, game tie-ins, community quests and future product launches.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section split-grid">
    <div class="panel-card">
      <span class="kicker">Brand position</span>
      <h2>Underground, but organised.</h2>
      <p>
        The site needs to work like a serious brand hub without losing the rawness. That means clear pages, fast navigation, better SEO, better mobile layout and stronger reasons for people to stay.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="button primary" href={`${base}collections/`}>View collections</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="panel-card">
      <span class="kicker">What lives here</span>
      <ul class="list-clean">
        <li>Brand story and origin of the NO BALL GAMES identity.</li>
        <li>Project pages for art, collectibles, gaming, lore and community.</li>
        <li>Collector-facing sections for future drops, merch and one-of-one work.</li>
        <li>Search-friendly pages that give Google something real to index.</li>
        <li>A cleaner structure ready for images, case studies and launch updates.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>Core areas</h2>
      <p>Each area can grow into a deeper page as the project expands.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="project-grid">
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Projects</span>
        <h3>Creative brand hub</h3>
        <p>Campaigns, experiments, drops, art projects, game ideas and Web3-ready extensions under the NO BALL GAMES name.</p>
        <a class="button secondary" href={`${base}projects/`}>Open projects</a>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Lore</span>
        <h3>The sign becomes a world</h3>
        <p>A living archive for characters, factions, stories, symbols and the mythology behind the brand.</p>
        <a class="button secondary" href={`${base}lore/`}>Read lore</a>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Collections</span>
        <h3>Collectible culture</h3>
        <p>A clean area for NFTs, physical pieces, prints, clothing, digital drops and future collector releases.</p>
        <a class="button secondary" href={`${base}collections/`}>View collections</a>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Community</span>
        <h3>People over platforms</h3>
        <p>The movement needs a home for fans, collectors, artists, players, collaborators and supporters.</p>
        <a class="button secondary" href={`${base}community/`}>Join community</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
